.SH NAME
anpu-tools - See which security engines are ready to use


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu tools [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Report the status of ANPU's built-in engines and any optional
external integrations (nuclei). Built-in engines need no installation —
they are compiled into the anpu binary.

.PP
External binaries are version-pinned (see the recipes) and their install-
time sha256 is recorded locally; anpu tools verify audits the records and
refuses drifted binaries at run time.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tools


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


